        "original_id": "4441d095-75f9-50bd-a71b-a2c184d2e532",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies, St. Olaf College\n- People: Michael Bauman, Bernt Julius Muus\n- Places: Oxford\n- Topics: American colleges and universities linked to CMRS\n\nFacts:\n- St. Olaf College was founded in 1874 by a group of Norwegian-American immigrant pastors and farmers led by Pastor Bernt Julius Muus.\n- Among the American colleges and universities that have sent students to the Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies are The University of Georgia, Elmhurst College, St. Mary's College of California, St. Mary's College of Maryland, St. Olaf College, William Jewell College, and Middlebury College.\n- Michael Bauman was a Lecturer and Tutor in Renaissance theology and literature at the Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies in Oxford for eight years.\n- Michael Bauman also served as Associate Dean of the Summer School at the Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies in Oxford.",
